g it is going to  cause quarterbacks to get overdrafted  this year and and i think the tension  will be between the scouts who will look  at kyler murray and say this is not  going to work this is not going to  happen this guy is not nearly big enough  strong enough thick enough to thrive at  the nfl level but then you're gonna have  a jimmy haslem who waltzes into the room  and and you know  says hey uh this is what we're doing i  own the team and owners get involved all  the time and make these picks and  influence these picks you don't have to  make the pick it's one of the privileges  of being a billionaire it's very easy to  influence what the people who work for  you do you don't have to say much you  don't have to drop a lot of hints to get  them to understand what you want but i  think that's what happens now we gotta  look at the teams that need quarterbacks  but the teams that need quarterbacks or  the teams that have older quarterbacks  and they want to get on this bandwagon  of having a young guy who's going to be  around for the next 10 or 15 years those  are the hot spots i don't disagree with  that but i still think big cat there's  there's a spot maybe in round you know  it's if he's not a top 10 top 12 top 15  pick  i i  i think he's going to reserve the right  deep down he's never going to say it but  i think deep down there's still that  chance to go back to baseball if he's  not thrilled with how the draft plays  out for him personally well of course  there's always a chance that he could go  back to baseball because that like when  you're thinking about kylo murray and  his decision of what to do you can't go  play baseball and and then say it's not  working out i can't hit a curveball i'm  gonna go play football you can play  football and then do the tim tebow and  later in your life say i'm gonna go try  baseball it probably won't work out  because he needs years and years of uh  you know hitting and batting practice  and being in the minors  